 # UnderWeb X changelog
 
+## 0.6.1-rc20 — Now showing, your crew, photos to the showcase
+
+- **Now showing** (OSC Lab → new chatbox module): what the world's video player is playing, e.g. "🍿 Now showing: Static Hearts". Tokens for title, who queued it (off by default), time, length, time left and a progress bar. Read from VRChat's log — links are never put in the chatbox, only a title (or "a YouTube video" if VRCX has no YouTube API key). Hides itself when you leave the instance. Every chatbox theme has a matching layout.
+- **Event Mode**: Music Video Night and Cinema Night switch "Now showing" on for the event and back off after. A new switch per preset.
+- **Your crew** (Command): the people you actually hang out with over the last 30 days, worked out from VRCX's own history on this PC (nothing uploaded). Shows who's with you, in VRChat, on the website or offline; one-click **Invite** or **Invite crew** for everyone online elsewhere (uses your invite message); pin people (also from the Lobby) or hide them. Optional pop-up when one of them comes online, with an Invite button. Labeled people never appear.
+- **Post to your showcase** (Command): send a VRChat photo (latest, or pick one) to your profile on underweb.cloud with a title and caption — it goes into the same staff review queue as website uploads. During an event the title is filled in for you. Optional "Post…" pop-up after every photo (off by default). **Privacy:** VRCX saves the world, the exact instance and everyone in the lobby inside each photo; UWX re-draws the picture into a fresh JPEG so none of that is uploaded. Needs your UnderWeb sign-in (System tab) and approved network access.
+
 ## 0.6.0-rc19 — Themes: client + chatbox
 
 - **Client themes** (System → Appearance): UnderWeb Green (default), Blood Moon, Violet, Ice, Gold, Rose, Mono, or any custom color. One accent recolors the whole client — UnderWeb pages, premium cards, and VRCX's own buttons, highlights and sidebar — with readable button text on any color. Optional background tint (none / subtle / strong). Turn it off to use VRCX's own theme. Saved on this PC and painted at startup with no flash.
